     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S4072\n\nSPONSOR: STEC\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authorization\ngranted to the county of Essex to impose an additional one percent of\nsales and compensating use taxes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend Essex County's authorization for its additional sales and\ncompensating tax for an additional two years.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 - Amends clause 36 of subparagraph (i) of the opening para-\ngraph of section 1210 of the tax law to provide authorization for Essex\nCounty to extend its additional one-percent sales and compensating tax.\n\nSection 2 - Provides effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nOn Jan. 4, 2023, the Essex County board voted unanimously to approve a\nresolution seeking legislation that would extend its authority to impose\nan additional one-percent sales tax. The county's existing authority is\ndue to expire on Dec. 1, 2023.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
